  "notes": "Audit, modified cash basis, FYE 9/30/2023. Governmental funds: General, Special Revenue (Street, Keno, ARPA sub-columns) and Debt Service; business-type: Sewer and Water enterprise fund. Statement lines from Exhibit D Total Governmental Funds (p5); State receipts 70,399.81 split by the Exhibit G state sources breakdown (p8), its 'Other state sources' 5,097.42 further by the fund schedules (homestead, carline); Other general receipts 64,004.73 split by fund schedules (p10-11); Capital outlay 31,199.82 split by function per Exhibit G (p9). Business-type lines from the Statement of Activities (p2-3), roll-forward from p3: -72,465.35 + 57,883.81 - 26,384.98 = -40,966.52. Governmental fund balance: 1,001,575.92 + 286,883.14 - 229,403.01 + 24,211.89 - 24,211.89 = 1,059,056.05. No prior-year cash printed, so beginning_cash null; ending_cash = cash in bank + county treasurer (p4), CDs in ending_investments. Detail from the departmental analyses (Exhibits H-K, p10-13); the Exhibit G budgetary comparison (p8-9, all funds combined, different allocation: transfer shown as General government 'Other', debt service split between street and sewer/water) is not recorded in detail to avoid double counting. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
